# Seven-lens audit protocol

When the user asks to run, fix, verify, close, or continue a seven-lens cycle:

1. Read `docs/cursor-seven-lens-audit-workflow.md` and
   `docs/cursor-seven-lens-prompts.md` before acting.
2. Run `python tools/seven_lens_protocol.py plan --cycle <N> --output
   docs/seven-lens-reports/cycle-<NN>-record.json` before reading source.
3. Work in exactly one role per chat: AUDITOR, FIXER, VERIFIER, or CLOSER.
   Stop at the role boundary. Never describe your own fix pass as independent.
4. The AUDITOR is read-only for application source and tests. Complete every
   generated part and every L1-L7 record before proposing fixes.
5. The FIXER implements only recorded findings and adds isolated behavioral
   evidence. Every probe must restore state in `finally`.
6. The VERIFIER uses a fresh chat/context, reads final source rather than relying
   on the fix summary, and reproduces the original failure through the user/API
   entry path.
7. The CLOSER runs `python tools/seven_lens_protocol.py check --phase close
   --record <record>` and may close only on exit 0.
8. Green automated tests are evidence, not a seven-lens review. Never infer "no
   bugs" or `SEVEN_LENS_REVIEWED` from test results alone.
9. Work against `dev`. Never target or modify `main` for this audit program.

